Original responses in rent_navigator/corpus/raw are retained without editing.
The statute responses are the full JSON documents served by the canonical
e-Laws pages' official API, including their complete HTML content. Canonical
citation URLs remain the public statute URLs, not the transport endpoints.

The text files are faithful, normalized extractions of the complete source
documents. Web navigation is excluded; headings, paragraphs and legal numbering
are retained, including the extracted PDF page text. Statutory
future-amendment annotations remain in full text but are excluded from operative
chunks. The index contains only the sections specified in CONTRACTS.md.
Source dates, consolidation periods and exact response/text hashes are recorded
in corpus/manifest.json. Historical examples in instructions are not rewritten
as current examples. Project rule descriptions are separate from quoted text.

